.TH GIBCERT 1
.SH NAME
gibcert \- manage ACME and local CA certificates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gibcert
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
[\fB\-\-syslog\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gibcert
reads a declarative configuration, issues or renews certificates through ACME
or a local CA, stores canonical certificate material in a state directory, and
deploys changed files to configured service paths.
.PP
Global flags must appear before the command name.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR, \fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path to the config file. Defaults to the platform config path.
.TP
.B \-\-state\-dir \fIPATH\fR
Path to the state directory. Defaults to the platform state path.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-format \fIFORMAT\fR
Log format. Supported values are text and json. The default is text.
.TP
.B \-\-syslog
Also send logs to syslog.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help [\fICOMMAND\fR]
Show global usage or command-specific usage.
.TP
.B version
Print build version information.
.TP
.B check
Parse and validate the config, then run preflight checks.
.TP
.B plan
Show what apply would change.
.TP
.B apply [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Reconcile state and deployed files with the config. Prints a plan, confirms
externally visible ACME actions unless \fB\-\-yes\fR is set, issues or renews
due certificates, then deploys configured material.
.TP
.B issue [\fB\-\-new\-key\fR] \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Issue one configured certificate. \fB\-\-new\-key\fR forces certificate key
rotation even when the config uses key reuse.
.TP
.B renew [\fB\-\-max\-jitter\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-jitter\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
Renew due certificates and deploy changed material. The default ACME renewal
jitter is 5m. When before-expiry is unset, the renewal window is one third of
the current certificate lifetime, capped at 30 days. \fB\-\-no\-jitter\fR
disables jitter.
.TP
.B account rotate-key \fIACCOUNT\fR
Rotate an existing ACME account key using ACME account key rollover. The
account must already be registered locally. gibcert archives the previous
local account.key next to the new key. For implicit accounts created by
certificate ca references, use ca:<ca-name>.
.TP
.B ca list
List built-in and configured CA profiles.
.TP
.B ca show \fICA\fR
Show one CA profile and, for local CAs, its local status and canonical paths.
For ACME CAs, also fetch and print the directory metadata (terms of service,
website, ARI endpoint, whether external account binding is required, and
recognised CAA identities).
.TP
.B ca export [\fB\-\-der\fR] \fICA\fR
Write a local CA certificate to stdout, as PEM by default or as binary DER
with \fB\-\-der\fR.
.TP
.B dns-persist install [\fB\-\-print\fR] \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Install the dns-persist-01 standing TXT record for each name in the
certificate using the certificate's configured DNS provider. With
\fB\-\-print\fR, print the records without writing them. Wildcard names are
installed with policy=wildcard.
.TP
.B dns-persist check \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Look up the standing TXT record for each name in the certificate and verify
it authorizes the configured account at the configured CA. Wildcard names
require policy=wildcard.
.TP
.B tlsa reconcile \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Reconcile DANE TLSA records for one configured certificate using stored
canonical certificate material. This does not issue, renew, or deploy the
certificate; it republishes current and staged next-key TLSA records, removes
stale records known from metadata, and refreshes TLSA metadata.
.TP
.B deploy \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Deploy stored canonical material for one configured certificate.
.TP
.B revoke [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR] [\fB\-\-reissue\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Revoke a stored ACME certificate at the CA. \fB\-\-reissue\fR issues and
deploys a replacement with a new key.
.TP
.B delete [\fB\-\-undeploy\fR] [\fB\-\-revoke\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIREASON\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Remove local certificate state. \fB\-\-undeploy\fR removes previously deployed
files only when their content still matches gibcert metadata.
.TP
.B rename \fIOLD-NAME\fR \fINEW-NAME\fR
Rename stored certificate state and update the stored metadata name. This does
not edit the configuration file; if the old name is still configured, gibcert
prints a warning.
.TP
.B list
List configured certificates with compact certificate, issuer, renewal, and
deploy status.
.TP
.B show \fICERTIFICATE\fR
Show one configured certificate, its status, issuer/account context, renewal
timing, stored metadata, canonical paths, TLSA state, and deploy targets with
per-file status.
.TP
.B import acme.sh [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fINAME\fR]... [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] \fIPATH\fR
Import certificate material from an acme.sh state directory. The
\fB\-\-only\fR selector matches either the acme.sh directory name or the
default gibcert target name, such as example.com_ecc or example.com-ecc.
\fB\-\-name\fR overrides the gibcert state name when exactly one certificate
is selected.
.TP
.B import certbot [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fINAME\fR]... [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] \fIPATH\fR
Import certificate material from a Certbot state directory (typically
/etc/letsencrypt). Scans live/ for certificate directories, reads the
leaf certificate, private key, and chain from symlinks, and extracts
the ACME directory URL from renewal/<name>.conf.
.TP
.B import dehydrated [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fINAME\fR]... [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] \fIPATH\fR
Import certificate material from a dehydrated base directory. Scans
certs/ for per-certificate directories, reads cert.pem, privkey.pem,
and chain.pem following symlinks, and extracts the ACME directory URL
from the config file.
.TP
.B import lego [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fINAME\fR]... [\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] \fIPATH\fR
Import certificate material from a lego state directory (typically .lego).
Scans certificates/ for key files and reads companion .crt and .issuer.crt
files. When .issuer.crt is present, it is used as the chain; otherwise
the .crt file is split into leaf and chain.
.TP
.B import pem [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR (\fB\-\-cert\fR \fICERT\fR [\fB\-\-chain\fR \fICHAIN\fR] | \fB\-\-fullchain\fR \fIFULLCHAIN\fR)
Import explicit PEM certificate material. gibcert derives names, serial
number, validity, and expiry from the leaf certificate. Renewal configuration,
ACME account settings, challenges, and deploy targets still come from the
configuration file.
.SH REVOCATION REASONS
Supported revocation reasons are unspecified, key-compromise, ca-compromise,
affiliation-changed, superseded, cessation-of-operation, certificate-hold,
privilege-withdrawn, and aa-compromise.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/gibcert/gibcert.scfg
Default config path for root on FHS-style Unix systems.
.TP
.I /var/lib/gibcert
Default state directory for root on FHS-style Unix systems.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIBCERT_CONFIG
Override the config path.
.TP
.B GIBCERT_STATE_DIR
Override the state directory.
.TP
.B GIBCERT_RUNTIME_DIR
Override the runtime directory.
.TP
.B GIBCERT_CACHE_DIR
Override the cache directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error, config error, validation error, or cancelled confirmation.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or unsupported flag value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gibcert.scfg (5)
